WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.459
If you want to hear the secrets behind the
demon that possessed the Annabelle doll then

00:00:03.459 --> 00:00:05.470
stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.840
I don't know why I'm doing this.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.320
I hope you weren’t tired of possessed doll
movies after all those Child’s Play episodes

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.460
I just released, because playtime is not over
quite yet.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:21.920
Today on Things You Missed, I’ll be covering
Annabelle.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:25.560
Annabelle is a series spun-off of James Wan’s
The Conjuring, and this story contains plenty

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.220
of covert references, easter eggs and links
to real world mythology.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.760
We’ll start at the chronological beginning
-- where the opening title is displayed over

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:37.430
this demonic looking statue.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.719
This guy looks exactly like Malthus, the actual
demon that Mia first discovers in the storage

00:00:41.719 --> 00:00:45.399
area -- so I think that this guy, like his
counterpart Valak from The Nun, has been around

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:50.579
for a long long time, and someone many years
ago encountered this demon and made the statue

00:00:50.579 --> 00:00:51.640
to depict him.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:54.260
The father gives his sermon where he tells
of the commandment,

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:57.580
“That you love one another as I have loved
you.

00:00:58.809 --> 00:01:05.200
Greater love hath no one than this: that he
lay down his life for his friends.”

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:09.160
This is a foreshadowing of the end of the
movie where, Evelyn does just that -- gives

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:11.570
up her life to try to save John and Mia’s
baby.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:15.220
After the church service, Mia goes to find
her neighbor, Sharon Higgins.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:16.520
Roll it.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.680
“Pete send you after me?

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:25.440
I swear he thinks one day I’ll just run
off too...”

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.710
Although we don’t know it yet, she’s talking
about their daughter, Annabelle Higgins, who

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:29.740
ran away as a teenager.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:34.500
"A man and his wife were brutally stabbed to
death my their estranged daughter, Annabelle

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.900
Higgins, and her unidentified boyfriend."

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.610
John later mentions that she had run off to
join up with the hippies, but she actually

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:43.590
left to join up with a cult known as the Disciples
of Ram.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:48.060
If you listen to the TV playing in the background
at the house, it reveals more about this cult:

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:51.620
They call themselves the family, but police
officials have labeled them as a dangerous

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:52.620
cult.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.120
Residing on the grounds of Spahn Ranch, the
family is estimated to have close to 30 members

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:00.660
who are responsible for the Tate and LaBianca
murders, their leader is Charles Manson and

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.370
they are involved in Satanic activities.

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:07.060
There are a couple of instances in Annabelle
where the TV predicts what’s going to happen

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.429
next, and this is one of them.

00:02:08.429 --> 00:02:12.409
The runaway Annabelle Higgins brings another
cult member along as they kill her parents,

00:02:12.409 --> 00:02:14.790
then go next door to attack the pregnant Mia.

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:18.129
One more important detail: Annabelle dies
with the doll in her arms, giving off the

00:02:18.129 --> 00:02:20.750
illusion that she transferred the demon into
Annabelle.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:24.200
In the prequel Annabelle: Creation, we find
out about how Annabelle Higgins was possessed

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.430
by the demon, but that doesn’t explain how
John ended up with the doll.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:31.540
He gives it to his wife as a gift, but doesn’t
really explain where he found it.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:32.920
"Where did you find her?

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.500
I mean... you know how long I've been looking?"

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.500
"I know."

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:38.880
"I'd completely lost hope."

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:40.530
"I have my ways."

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.330
I don’t think this is a coincidence.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:46.220
We also don’t find out how the doll ended
up going from Evelyn’s dying arms to this

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.999
collectors shop at the end of the movie, or
how it got from the trash can to John’s

00:02:49.999 --> 00:02:54.129
new apartment -- so my theory is that the
demon is looking for families he thinks are

00:02:54.129 --> 00:02:55.129
vulnerable.

00:02:55.129 --> 00:02:57.700
Mia and John were good candidates, because
she was already a doll collector and they

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:01.319
lived next door to the Higginses so they could
see the murders take place, and thus be more

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:03.810
likely to believe that something had possessed
the doll.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:06.779
Because remember, it’s explained at the
beginning of the Conjuring that the demon

00:03:06.779 --> 00:03:10.340
doesn’t really possess the doll, but just
moves it around to try to trick people into

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:11.489
offering up their souls.

00:03:11.489 --> 00:03:15.549
Annabelle is found dead holding the doll in
the nursery with this symbol on the wall.

00:03:15.549 --> 00:03:19.450
If you rotate it, it looks like the letter
A. This symbol re-appears throughout the movie:

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.989
like the scar on Mia’s arm after being attacked
by Malthus, and the one of the images in the

00:03:22.989 --> 00:03:26.430
book that Mia reads to investigate the occult
and the Disciples of Ram.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:30.079
The letter A also appears near the end of
the movie after the nursery has been attacked.

00:03:30.079 --> 00:03:33.879
There’s a big A block that was never there
before, and the baby’s name starts with

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:34.930
the letter L, not A.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:38.879
One more thing note on the attack, the cult
member accompanying Annabelle has a Ram belt

00:03:38.879 --> 00:03:42.999
buckle, an early clue that the cult is, in
fact, performing some kind of ritual involving

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:48.680
Malthus, as the detective puts it later on,
“Their act wasn’t devotional, they were

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.200
they were actually trying to ‘Conjure’ something
up.”

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.230
“Like what?”

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:58.609
“The devil, demons, the tooth fairy, I don't
know specifically.”

00:03:58.609 --> 00:04:01.599
I can’t wait for the Conjuring spin-off
on the tooth fairy.

00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:03.500
I’m turning up on day 1 for that one.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.109
Let’s look at some of the repeated symbols
throughout the house.

00:04:06.109 --> 00:04:09.610
We see this a lot in the movies we cover here
on Things You Missed, but there are a tons

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:11.560
of flower images decorating the house.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:14.169
We keep seeing them over and over and over
and over again.

00:04:14.169 --> 00:04:17.389
There are also a lot of butterfly images,
and when you put these together, you have

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:21.190
a pollination and fertility metaphor, which
goes along with the newborn baby being the

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:22.750
central focus of this film.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:26.919
The other symbol I saw a ton of in the house
was owls, these are hidden everywhere.

00:04:26.919 --> 00:04:30.460
They show up so much that I have no doubt
they are meant to be noticed, but how you

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:31.590
interpret them may vary.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:36.650
I see them as mysterious nocturnal creatures,
much like the demons of the Conjuring universe.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:40.250
Owls are also often seen as symbols of wisdom,
and Father Perez later tells them that the

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.419
more they know about their enemies, the less
they will fear them.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:47.980
“Isn't it true that the more we know about
something the less fear we have from it.

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:53.360
We need to face our fears to better understand
them."

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.780
The great thing about the father is that he
always talks like that.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:56.889
Like even in a regular conversation.

00:04:56.889 --> 00:04:58.889
Imagine if I did that in my videos.

00:04:58.889 --> 00:05:04.090
Here lies, the things you missed, that have
been bestowed upon us by the director John

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:06.289
Leonetti, who also made Mortal Kombat Annihilation.

00:05:06.289 --> 00:05:07.289
I’m done.

00:05:07.289 --> 00:05:08.289
I’m ****ing done.

00:05:08.289 --> 00:05:11.919
After the demon starts a fire that burns up
the house, Mia has the baby and they move

00:05:11.919 --> 00:05:13.490
into the Palmeri Apartments.

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:17.530
The name Palmeri refers to the cleric who
carries a palm branch in religious ceremonies,

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:19.530
another tie into the religious themes of the
movie.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:23.600
The doll somehow follows them there, and as I
mentioned earlier, some satanic symbols start

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:24.600
to show up.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:28.520
I think these light ballasts resemble the
number 6, and there seem to be 3 of them:

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:29.520
666.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:33.030
They also live on the sixth floor, and when
Mia encounters Malthus downstairs, she gets

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:35.640
into the elevator and mashes the 6 button
three times.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:38.350
This scene also gives us our best look at
Malthus.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:42.610
We usually only see him manipulating the Annabelle
doll and occasionally using the forms of Annabelle

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:43.610
Higgins.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.990
As I did for Valak in my video on The Nun,
I’ll bring up the lights so we can get a

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.319
better look at the true form.

00:05:48.319 --> 00:05:52.150
This demon seems to have claw like hands and
the ability to climb on walls or ceilings.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:55.710
You also may have also missed the demon hiding
behind the curtain when Mia turns off the

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:56.560
record player.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:08.880
If you pause when Mia is flipping through
The Devil’s Welcome, the book which is basically

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.360
the movie equivalent of The Lesser Key of
Solomon, you can find more information

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:14.720
about Malthus and the Disciples of Ram.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.729
To put it into easy to understand terms, it
basically says that there are rules, and you

00:06:18.729 --> 00:06:21.910
have to agree to give up your soul to this
demon before he can possess you.

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:26.100
If you do, it’s everlasting, so there’s
no going back on it, no crossed fingers clause,

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.310
nothing to get you out of this deal.

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:29.860
The making of this deal is something that
the church fears.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:33.580
The Disciples can summon the demon by shedding
one’s blood, which is what we saw at the

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:37.560
beginning of the movie, but this is only to
be done as a sacrifice to Malthus, and not

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:41.639
for food, unless this is meat given to them
by the demon specifically for food.

00:06:41.639 --> 00:06:45.150
And he basically wants to take over every
living creature on earth eventually.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:49.379
The picture depicts the detail that we eventually
learn from Father Perez, that a baby doesn’t

00:06:49.379 --> 00:06:52.419
really know how to agree to give up it’s
soul, so it could be potentially an easier

00:06:52.419 --> 00:06:55.340
target -- though that doesn’t seem to be
the case for Lia.

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:57.840
Flipping through some of the other pages of
The Devil’s Welcome, we can see some other

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.379
connections and other demons.

00:06:59.379 --> 00:07:02.540
The image of the snake eating its tail is
something that’s seen many times in connection

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:06.599
with Valak, the marquis of snakes, who appears
in The Conjuring 2 and The Nun, alongside

00:07:06.599 --> 00:07:07.860
that same image of the snake.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.801
There’s also an illustration of Beleth,
the Mighty King of Hell, and mention of Belial,

00:07:11.801 --> 00:07:13.969
the demon without a master.

00:07:13.969 --> 00:07:16.949
On the next page there’s a Abaddon, the
angel of the abyss.

00:07:16.949 --> 00:07:20.580
Unfortunately, the page on the tooth fairy
is missing, but I think these are demons that

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:24.710
it does show are all good candidates to be
the antagonist of future Conjuring universe

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:25.710
movies.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:29.419
One of the other books on the shelf in Evelyn’s
store is called Ghosts, Spirits and Apparitions,

00:07:29.419 --> 00:07:30.800
by Anthony Astrino.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:34.460
Anthony Astrino is the name of a writer for
a series called The Mentalist, which is about

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:38.069
a famous psychic, much like Lorraine Warren
is in the this universe.

00:07:38.069 --> 00:07:40.759
This isn’t a real book by the way, they
just borrowed his name for it.

00:07:40.759 --> 00:07:45.410
The name of Father Perez’s apartment complex
is The Barclay, a reference to Andy Barclay,

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:49.330
the main character of the Child’s Play franchise,
which is the other major killer doll movie

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:52.409
series that exists, so nice to see them pay
a little homage.

00:07:52.409 --> 00:07:55.530
When they tell the Father of the occurrences
that have been going on, he says he doesn’t

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.610
know how to stop the demon, but someone at
the church might.

00:07:58.610 --> 00:07:59.789
Roll it.

00:07:59.789 --> 00:08:04.070
“At the very least, I’ve heard of a married
couple that the church has worked with in

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:06.560
the past that deal with this type of thing.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:09.659
They’re back east, but a call can always
be placed.”

00:08:09.659 --> 00:08:13.270
He’s referencing the Warrens, the main characters
of the mainline Conjuring films who live in

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:14.270
Connecticut.

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:17.319
Now, remember how I said the TV can be sign
of things to come?

00:08:17.319 --> 00:08:20.439
The General Hospital clip that plays while
Mia is asleep on the couch leads up to the

00:08:20.439 --> 00:08:23.580
sequence where Father Perez tries taking the
doll to the church with the belief that he

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:27.740
can weaken it that way, then get air yeeted
straight into the hospital, where John is

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:28.740
working.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:31.310
So that leaves Mia and Evelyn to fight off
the demon on her own.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:35.190
Mia is about to give the demon her soul in
exchange for her baby, but Evelyn sacrifices

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:39.930
herself instead, ‘that he lay down his life
for his friends’ or in this case, for her

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:40.930
friends.

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:43.849
However, as we know, all this does is transfers
the demon to someone else.

00:08:43.849 --> 00:08:46.130
Also, do they not get blamed for killing Evelyn?

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:48.639
I mean... maybe they should have thought that
one through a bit more.

00:08:48.639 --> 00:08:52.420
But we don’t see the scene where I’m assuming
Mia and John are taken away in handcuffs,

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:56.450
instead we skip forward a little under a year
to this woman entering a collectors’ shop.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:59.160
In the background, you can spot an actual
Raggedy Ann doll.

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:02.920
This is the supposedly haunted doll in the
real life that the movie is based on, but

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:06.260
because of licensing issues and in order to
make it look more creepy, they made Annabelle

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:07.680
a porcelain doll for the movies.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:10.280
This woman buys the doll for her daughter
who is a nurse.

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:13.180
"I'm just trying to find something for my
daughter.

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.240
Thanks.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:15.760
She's a nurse.

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:17.800
Always helping people."

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:21.410
The women who explain their paranormal experiences
with Annabelle in the opening scene of both

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:23.790
this movie and The Conjuring are the nurses.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.320
"I mean, we're nurses, we help people."

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:28.220
So one of them must be this woman’s daughter.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:32.050
I also find it interesting that we never see
the cashier who sells Annabelle to the old

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:33.050
woman on screen.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:37.200
Maybe the demon took over this cashier in
order pass on Annabelle to a new family, just

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:40.019
as John mysteriously found the doll his wife
was looking for.

00:09:40.019 --> 00:09:41.950
Let me know your thoughts on that in the comments.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:45.600
And make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld for
new horrors every week, because next week

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:48.070
I’ll be covering the prequel, Annabelle:
Creation.

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:52.000
Remember to ring that deathbell for notifications
and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:53.880
Assuming we both survive.

